1097|     /**
1098|      * Computes the n-th roots of this complex number.
1099|      * The nth roots are defined by the formula:
1100|      * <pre>
1101|      *  <code>
1102|      *   z<sub>k</sub> = abs<sup>1/n</sup> (cos(phi + 2&pi;k/n) + i (sin(phi + 2&pi;k/n))
1103|      *  </code>
1104|      * </pre>
1105|      * for <i>{@code k=0, 1, ..., n-1}</i>, where {@code abs} and {@code phi}
1106|      * are respectively the {@link #abs() modulus} and
1107|      * {@link #getArgument() argument} of this complex number.
1108|      * <br/>
1109|      * If one or both parts of this complex number is NaN, a list with just
1110|      * one element, {@link #NaN} is returned.
1111|      * if neither part is NaN, but at least one part is infinite, the result
1112|      * is a one-element list containing {@link #INF}.
